      "treatment_summary": "Single dose of prednisolone (PSL) effective for fever; at 4 years 2 months PSL not effective for a 9-day fever; fever often improved without antibiotics; tonsillectomy, after which the frequency of fever episodes decreased; treated with cimetidine at the time of flow cytometry analysis.",
      "disease_label_as_stated": "PFAPA (periodic fever, aphthous stomatitis, pharyngitis, and adenitis) syndrome (diagnosis before the identification of TNFAIP3 variants); suspected case of HA20",
      "clinical_diagnosis_basis": "PFAPA diagnosed based on Thomas's criteria, prednisolone effective for fever; initially suspected immunodeficiency but neutrophil function, lymphocyte fraction and immunoglobulin levels normal. TNFAIP3 variant found by target gene sequencing (400-gene primary immunodeficiency panel) and confirmed by Sanger sequencing; did not fulfill diagnostic criteria of BD.",
